{
  "version": 1,
  "questionId": "q03",
  "speechText": "For me, I do not just blame the LLM when something goes wrong. I check the whole workflow to find the real root cause. That's because a bad result can come from bad input, wrong retrieval, backend logic, prompt construction, the AI provider, or the model itself. For example, for temporary failures like network errors, timeouts, or some 5xx errors, I use a bounded retry. If one model is down, I may use a fallback model. But for bad credentials or bad requests, I fail fast. So first, I separate temporary errors from permanent errors. Then I decide: retry, fail, or fall back. I also track the request or job ID, the model, latency, retry count, error type, token usage, and which workflow step failed. So overall, I look for the real root cause, choose the right strategy for each error, and keep the workflow easy to monitor and debug.",
